new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/asm-destructor-start.s
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+.syntax unified
+.arm
+.section .text.start
+.global _start
+_start:
+    ldr r3, =main
+    mov lr, pc
+    bx r3
+    mov r7, #1
+    svc #0
+.thumb
+.thumb_func
+.global _call_via_r1
+_call_via_r1:
+    bx r1
+.thumb_func
+.global _call_via_r2
+_call_via_r2:
+    bx r2
diff --git a/tests/README.asm-destructor.md b/tests/README.asm-destructor.md
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/README.asm-destructor.md
@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+# Asm-labelled destructor regression
+
+GNU C++ permits a destructor declaration to select a different assembler
+symbol. The source-level destructor kind must survive that name replacement.
+The old frontend instead identifies destructors by their mangled assembler
+name: an out-of-line definition can be rejected, and a declared external
+destructor can silently disappear from automatic cleanup.
+
+The correction stores that kind in the existing spare declaration-flag bit
+and uses it in method lookup, cleanup, overriding and diagnostics. The old
+name test remains for synthesized declarations. Both ARM and Thumb C++
+frontends receive the same change; instruction selection and optimization
+options are unchanged. No game address or function-specific rule is involved.
+
+`asm-destructor.cc` checks reverse stack destruction, array destruction,
+virtual dispatch plus deleting destruction, and destruction of an
+asm-labelled member in an ordinary template holder. It does not test or
+claim support for attaching asm labels to template destructor instantiations.
+
+After the normal `./build.sh`, the following commands run the regression
+under Linux with `arm-none-eabi` binutils and `qemu-arm`:
+
+```sh
+tmpdir=$(mktemp -d)
+arm-none-eabi-cpp -P tests/asm-destructor.cc > "$tmpdir/test.i"
+arm-none-eabi-as -mcpu=arm7tdmi tests/asm-destructor-start.s -o "$tmpdir/start.o"
+for mode in thumb arm; do
+    if [ "$mode" = thumb ]; then
+        compiler=./agbcp
+    else
+        compiler=./agbcp_arm
+    fi
+    "$compiler" -quiet -fno-exceptions -fno-rtti -fvtable-thunks \
+        -mthumb-interwork -O2 -o "$tmpdir/$mode.s" < "$tmpdir/test.i"
+    arm-none-eabi-as -mcpu=arm7tdmi "$tmpdir/$mode.s" -o "$tmpdir/$mode.o"
+    arm-none-eabi-ld -Ttext=0x10000 -e _start "$tmpdir/start.o" \
+        "$tmpdir/$mode.o" -o "$tmpdir/$mode.elf"
+    qemu-arm "$tmpdir/$mode.elf" || exit "$?"
+done
+```
+
+Both executions must return zero. The original `cp` revision rejects the
+out-of-line `Leaf::~Leaf()` definition in the same source.
+
+## 中文说明
+
+GNU C++ 允许析构声明指定不同的汇编符号。旧前端依据汇编符号的
+名称识别析构函数，改名后会拒绝类外定义，或者静默漏掉自动析构。
+修复复用声明标志中已有的空闲位，保留源语言中的析构身份，并在
+查找、清理、虚函数覆盖和诊断中统一使用；旧名称判断仍为自动生成
+的声明保留。ARM、Thumb 两套前端同步修复，不改指令选择、优化
+选项，也不判断任何游戏函数或地址。
+
+上述测试实际执行栈对象逆序析构、数组析构、虚函数删除及模板成员
+析构，两种模式均应返回零。模板容器本身使用普通析构声明；此测试
+不声称支持为模板析构实例指定汇编名。
